    description: "FOUND 2026-10-25 (premise check of INV-kobad), verified on fixtures and in the grammar.\n\nDEFECT. analyze/cyclomatic.py's Ruby decision-point set is {if, unless, while, until, for, when, in_clause, rescue, ternary}. tree-sitter-ruby has no 'ternary' node: `a > b ? a : b` parses as `conditional`. The statement-modifier forms `x if a`, `x unless a`, `x while a`, `x until a`, `x rescue nil` parse as if_modifier, unless_modifier, while_modifier, until_modifier, rescue_modifier, none of which is listed.\n\nMEASURED. `def m(a, b); a > b ? a : b; end` -> cyclomatic_complexity 1 in Ruby, 2 for the same ternary in java, rust, js, c and python. A method containing `return 1 if a; x unless a; y while a` -> cc=1.\n\nFIX. Replace 'ternary' with 'conditional' and add the five *_modifier types (each is a single-condition construct, counted once, consistent with the set's comment). Guard against recurrence: assert every name in each language's set is a node type the grammar can produce (node-types.json), so a misnamed entry fails a test instead of silently counting 0.\n\nINV-kobad matrix row 1 (ruby column)."  # 563e
